{
  "uid": "dthcms-ai-quality",
  "title": "DTHCMS · AI quality",
  "description": "Whether the AI is safe to show a physician (CP72, §10.2, §10.5).\n\nRead it top to bottom. **Is anything ungrounded reaching us**, **is anybody looking at what the check refused**, and **is the frozen evaluation set still passing**.\n\nTwo panels exist to stop this dashboard lying to you and they are the ones to understand first.\n\n*Tokens the check examined* is the denominator. A grounding-violation count of zero from a check that examined nothing looks exactly like a healthy system, and a payload whose fact index stopped decoding would produce precisely that picture. If that panel goes flat, the clean rate above it means nothing.\n\n*False-positive rate* is **absent, never zero, until somebody has reviewed a defect**. A validator nobody has checked has an unknown false-positive rate; a gap in that panel means the review queue is not being worked, not that the check is never wrong.",
  "tags": ["dthcms", "ai", "quality", "grounding"],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "Asia/Dhaka",
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Ungrounded answers (24h)",
      "description": "Model answers refused because a claim in them could not be traced to what the model was shown. **Every one of these is a defect, not a retry** — the answer was thrown away and the physician saw the degraded screen. The target is zero reaching the physician, and since none of them do, this is really a measure of how often the model invents.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(dthcms_ai_grounding_checked{verdict=\"FAILED\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Open defects",
      "description": "Grounding violations nobody has classified yet. Not windowed: last week's unreviewed defect is still unreviewed. This is the backlog that makes the false-positive rate beside it unmeasurable.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(dthcms_ai_grounding_defects_open)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "False-positive rate (reviewed)",
      "description": "Of the defects a person has looked at, the fraction they judged the **check** wrong about rather than the model. Acceptance criterion 2, measured in production rather than on a frozen set.\n\n**No value means nobody has reviewed anything**, which is a different and worse state than zero. The gauge is deliberately not published until there is something to publish.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dthcms-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(dthcms_ai_grounding_false_positive_rate)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Evaluation set",
      "description": "1 when the last run of the frozen evaluation set passed its baseline, 0 when it failed. A **gap** means the harness has not run for this agent at all, which is how a CI gate stops being a gate without anybody deciding to remove it — see the age panel below.",
